+(duration-type)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole
+number of seconds, like `120`, or one or more groups of a whole number followed by a unit: `d` (days), `h` (hours),
+`m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may appear at most once, units must be given in that order, and there
+must be no spaces. Units are case-insensitive, so `2d`, `1h30m`, `45S`, and `1d2h3m4s` are all valid.
+
+Negative numbers, decimals, unknown units, and repeated or out of order units are rejected.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Timeout: {timeout}")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+```
+
